# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env.local — keys and secrets for THIS deployment. Copy to `.env.local`, or run
# `npm run setup`. Never committed. Non-secret instance settings live in `.env`
# (template: `.env.example`).
#
# Variable names must be bare — `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=...`, not
# `"PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL"=...`. A quoted or backticked name is silently ignored by
# Vite, and because analytics fails soft that looks exactly like "no events yet".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase — Project Settings → API (cloud), or `supabase status` (local CLI),
# or your self-hosted stack's API URL + ANON_KEY.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Optional, SERVER-ONLY. Lets the Resend webhook update the email log without RLS,
# and lets `npm run setup` create the first platform admin. Never prefix with
# PUBLIC_ — that would ship it to every browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# PostHog — product analytics + error tracking (optional).
# Leave unset and analytics silently no-ops; nothing else breaks.
# The key is a PUBLIC, write-only ingest key (phc_...) — safe in the browser
# bundle. Never put a personal API key (phx_...) here.
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Email (Resend) is NOT configured here. The send paths are Supabase Edge
# Functions, so their secrets are Edge Function secrets:
#   supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#   supabase secrets set LUMA_FROM_EMAIL="Your Org Recruiting <recruiting@yourdomain.com>"
# Without RESEND_API_KEY the functions run in dry-run mode and only report how
# many emails would have been sent.
